B4.18 · loop back to: Any candidates left?  ^9O68lJfz

The key is the literal text "DUMMY_KEY" and requests go to a local address on this machine, not to Google. If nothing is listening there, it fails and lands on B4.13 every time. ^R9If0Idf

Unlike B3, an engine failure here is swallowed by the silent skip. And because the "already run" flag is only set after it succeeds, a failing engine is retried for every remaining candidate. ^xZxq3fzm

